        "Content": "Hume Auctioneers ? We Get The Pick Of The Crop.\n\nSet on a stunning elevated site in the foothills of the Slieve Bloom mountains yes just minutes from Portlaoise and surrounding towns, this breathtakingly beautiful home is picture perfect throughout and sits on a magnificent 1.6 Acre site.\n\nThe ground-floor accommodation is exceptionally spacious, bright and beautifully presented throughout. A contemporary front door with glazed side panels opens into an impressive reception hallway, featuring high-gloss tiled flooring and an elegant handcrafted staircase.\n\nThe superb open-plan kitchen/living/dining room extends to approximately 8.55m × 5.80m and forms the heart of the home. The kitchen is fitted with an extensive range of stylish Shaker-style units, marble-effect worktops, glazed display cabinets, feature wine storage and a range-style cooker. The adjoining living and dining areas offer excellent space for both family life and entertaining, with a feature fireplace and large glazed doors opening directly onto the patio and gardens.\n\nA separate sitting room provides an additional generous reception space and is presently arranged as a games and family room. The large utility/laundry room is exceptionally well fitted, with extensive storage and dedicated space for appliances.\n\nThe versatile home office is currently used as a salon and would also be ideal as a study, treatment room or hobby room. A beautifully finished ground-floor shower room features contemporary tiling, a large walk-in rainfall shower, wash-hand basin and WC. A substantial hot press completes the ground-floor accommodation.\n\nThe first floor is arranged around an exceptionally spacious and light-filled landing, beautifully finished with contemporary flooring, a feature chandelier and an attractive balustrade overlooking the staircase. There are four generously proportioned bedrooms, including an impressive main bedroom with a stylish ensuite shower room. One of the bedrooms is presently used as an extensive dressing room, perfectly demonstrating the versatility of the accommodation. A superb family bathroom, luxuriously appointed with a bath and separate shower enclosure, completes this outstanding level.\n\nA drop-down ladder leads to a massive fully floored walkaround attic.\n\nOutside the grounds are stunningly beautiful. With wraparound lawns and a gorgeous rear paddock, this home truly appreciates its setting. The entire is 1.6 Acres of glorious countryside.\nAnd what about those views. Fields, townlands and counties, roll along as far as the eye can see passing over towns and villages to faraway mountains. It is a spectacle that must be viewed to be fully appreciated.\n\nThere are two exceptional and spacious garages of steel construction. The larger spans to 82 Square Metres and the second to 26 Square Metres. They are meticulously finished and fully wired.\n\nPark View House has been constructed to a standard seldom found in today?s market. \nAmong the details are:\n? Electric gate\n? House wired for a generator as a backup\n? 60 double sockets throughout the house\n? 3 outdoor sockets\n? External lighting\n? Concrete-clad stairs\n? 50 mm insulated slab boards on all external walls, including the upstairs ceilings\n? 200 mm Kingspan insulation under the ground floor and the same in the cavity walls\n? 400 mm Rockwool insulation throughout the attic\n? Stira folding attic stairs\n? Sheds electrically wired; the large shed has an automatic roller door\n? Fibre broadband\n\nThe impressive B1 energy rating reflects the tremendous attention paid to insulation, construction detail and overall build quality throughout the home. This high level of energy efficiency ensures a warmer, more comfortable living environment, significantly reduced energy bills and the potential to qualify for preferential green mortgage interest rates?a valuable benefit for today?s discerning buyer.\n\nViewing of this spectacular home is highly recommended.\n"
